explicit and refuse ambiguity. The inventory is large, about 680 KB, but it is evidence, not runtime code. No runtime code is added.\n\nVerification conclusion: with the planner's continuation ruling, the evidence covers this tree's code and tests. That evidence is the failed whole gate with its passing Vitest and Node 37 results, plus the Counting continuation at bcd244c5. Only F1 stands between this and approval.\n\nResidual risk: the preservation check compares the whole working tree with the recorded basis 235e9262. Once Main moves on, it will report unrelated paths. That is acceptable for a one-time review tool, but docs/workspace-rename.md could later say the check applies at the rename head; this is not required here. No public installation, registry publication or deployment is claimed or approved.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:deb715aeaf0b291a83279997a7f07022df48256c","binding":"assigned","head":"f499e537dcc0ed68d271f011aef34e989be09c19","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:41d4142da8da7f05a8da8fb3a9405100c94f44ae\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4fea38630cb36265d6d3f9108104e2af53805e39\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:eab39f74aef0873e89280e7cb5923616aaa0f72b","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}